    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9854" root="خبأ" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَابِئَةٌ</span></b> , as sometimes pronounced, (Msb,) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَابِيَةٌ</span>, with the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span> suppressed, (S, Msb, K,) because
of frequent usage, (Msb,) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُبٌّ</span> [q. v.]; (S,
K;) i. e. <i>A large jar:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خوابى</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَوَابِئُ</span>,
or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَوَابٍ</span>]: (TA:) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَبَأَهُ</span> “ he hid it, ” or “ concealed it. ” (S, Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِنْتُ الخَابِيَةِ</span>
(assumed tropical:)  <i>Wine.</i> (Har p. 365.)

